     "text": "{\"count\": 1, \"rationale\": \"With no defences, exfiltration is reachable. Phishing gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. Pivot_internal gives reach_internal. Auth_appserver followed by kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin. Auth_dc and escalate_dc give admin_dc. Dump_dbadmin_dc gives stolen_dbadmin. Auth_db and escalate_db give admin_db, and exfiltrate_db succeeds. So at least one control is needed. Every exfiltration technique needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Those need a foothold from auth_db, auth_fileserver or auth_backup, and each of those requires stolen_dbadmin. The only sources of stolen_dbadmin are dump_dbadmin_dc and dump_dbadmin_adfs, which need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, and the only way to get either is auth_dc or auth_adfs, both of which require NOT mfa_admin. Deploying mfa:admin alone therefore blocks the entire chain, so the minimum is 1.\"}"
